LiteRT-LM v0.18.0, runtime/core/tasks.cc: when a speculative (MTP) step
returns several tokens and the stop token is not the last of them, roll back
only the tokens after it. Upstream rolls back the stop token too, so every
such turn ends without its stop token in the KV cache
(https://github.com/google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM/issues/3439).

Reference only, for upstream: the image applies the same fix to the PyPI
wheel's own library, one instruction (fix_mtp_rollback.py). A source build
can't use Google's prebuilt tool-call constraint provider, which the wheel's
library has built in.

diff --git a/runtime/core/tasks.cc b/runtime/core/tasks.cc
index 4ea8174f..2caf075d 100644
--- a/runtime/core/tasks.cc
+++ b/runtime/core/tasks.cc
@@ -334,8 +334,14 @@ class DecodeOneStep {
       if (all_done) {
         if (step != sequence_length - 1) {
           // we are done before all the tokens are processed, so we need to
-          // rollback the processed tokens in executor.
-          int diff = sequence_length - step;
+          // rollback the processed tokens in executor. Only the tokens after
+          // the stop token go: the executor's step counts its pending input
+          // token, and the stop token must stay as that pending token so the
+          // next prefill commits it to the KV cache, as it does when it comes
+          // last (always, without speculative decoding). Rolling it back too
+          // left every speculative turn without its stop token
+          // (google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM#3439).
+          int diff = sequence_length - step - 1;
           ABSL_ASSIGN_OR_RETURN(int current_step, executor_.GetCurrentStep());
           ABSL_RETURN_IF_ERROR(executor_.SetCurrentStep(current_step - diff));
         }
